  "vo": [
    {
      "id": "V1",
      "text": "That's Mrs. Lan. Power out two days since the ice storm. She doesn't read English. She just left a voice note for her neighborhood hotline. Watch the clock.",
      "start": "0:03.5",
      "end": "0:12.0",
      "window": 8.5,
      "words": 28,
      "wpm": 150,
      "estSeconds": 11.2,
      "fits": false,
      "needWpm": 198
    },
    {
      "id": "V2",
      "text": "She heard it read back in Vietnamese and said yes. The group's own rules, not the AI, set the amount: a hundred and fifty dollars. Two organizers, on two phones.",
      "start": "0:12.5",
      "end": "0:24.0",
      "window": 11.5,
      "words": 30,
      "wpm": 150,
      "estSeconds": 12,
      "fits": false,
      "needWpm": 157
    },
    {
      "id": "V3",
      "text": "Paid, into her Venmo, with a message in Vietnamese. Twenty-two point three seconds from voice note to the SUCCESS webhook, on our PayPal stand-in. Our organizers tapped on cue; with real volunteers, it's as long as two neighbors take to check their phones.",
      "start": "0:32.0",
      "end": "0:45.8",
      "window": 13.8,
      "words": 43,
      "wpm": 160,
      "estSeconds": 16.13,
      "fits": false,
      "needWpm": 187
    },
    {
      "id": "V4",
      "text": "This is Neighborline: a hotline, not a dashboard. After the Eaton fire, one LA mutual-aid network took three hundred requests overnight, in Instagram comments. Most groups still run on spreadsheets and a volunteer's personal Venmo.",
      "start": "0:46.3",
      "end": "1:00.0",
      "window": 13.7,
      "words": 35,
      "wpm": 150,
      "estSeconds": 14,
      "fits": false,
      "needWpm": 153
    },
    {
      "id": "V5a",
      "text": "Rosa asks for groceries, in Spanish. Same rules, two approvals.",
      "start": "1:01.0",
      "end": "1:05.0",
      "window": 4,
      "words": 10,
      "wpm": 150,
      "estSeconds": 4,
      "fits": true,
      "needWpm": 150
    },
    {
      "id": "V5b",
      "text": "Her email has no PayPal account yet, so PayPal reports the payout unclaimed.",
      "start": "1:12.4",
      "end": "1:17.6",
      "window": 5.2,
      "words": 13,
      "wpm": 150,
      "estSeconds": 5.2,
      "fits": true,
      "needWpm": 150
    },
    {
      "id": "V5c",
      "text": "Most systems stop there. Neighborline messages her, in Spanish, exactly how to claim it.",
      "start": "1:18.0",
      "end": "1:23.0",
      "window": 5,
      "words": 14,
      "wpm": 155,
      "estSeconds": 5.42,
      "fits": false,
      "needWpm": 168
    },
    {
      "id": "V5d",
      "text": "She does. Success.",
      "start": "1:23.2",
      "end": "1:25.5",
      "window": 2.3,
      "words": 3,
      "wpm": 150,
      "estSeconds": 1.2,
      "fits": true,
      "needWpm": 78
    },
    {
      "id": "V6",
      "text": "Someone posing as the organizers, with a Venmo handle one letter off? Approve is disabled on every phone. No money moves.",
      "start": "1:28.0",
      "end": "1:36.0",
      "window": 8,
      "words": 21,
      "wpm": 155,
      "estSeconds": 8.13,
      "fits": false,
      "needWpm": 158
    },
    {
      "id": "V7a",
      "text": "Under the hood: the agents that talk to neighbors have no PayPal tools at all. One separate approval service holds the Payouts credentials, and it pays only on a record signed with the passkeys of two different organizers.",
      "start": "1:36.3",
      "end": "1:50.0",
      "window": 13.7,
      "words": 38,
      "wpm": 165,
      "estSeconds": 13.82,
      "fits": false,
      "needWpm": 166,
      "note": "Retimed: the script gives part 1 only 1:36–1:46 (37 words = 222 wpm). It now runs into Shot 10."
    },
    {
      "id": "V7b",
      "text": "Every AI output is checked against a schema, repaired once, or the neighbor is asked again, never guessed.",
      "start": "1:50.3",
      "end": "1:57.6",
      "window": 7.3,
      "words": 18,
      "wpm": 165,
      "estSeconds": 6.55,
      "fits": true,
      "needWpm": 148,
      "note": "Retimed: runs over code card 1, which is the schema-repair card it describes."
    },
    {
      "id": "V7c",
      "text": "The batch ID is a hash of that approval, so a double tap can't pay twice. Webhooks are signature-verified, and every payout is reconciled against PayPal Transaction Search.",
      "start": "1:58.0",
      "end": "2:11.5",
      "window": 13.5,
      "words": 28,
      "wpm": 155,
      "estSeconds": 10.84,
      "fits": true,
      "needWpm": 124
    },
    {
      "id": "V8",
      "text": "Donors give with PayPal or Venmo. The public report is AI-written around numbers that code pulls from the ledger, and it never names a neighbor. Built for the roughly nine hundred volunteer groups that mobilize when the storm hits.",
      "start": "2:12.3",
      "end": "2:29.5",
      "window": 17.2,
      "words": 39,
      "wpm": 150,
      "estSeconds": 15.6,
      "fits": true,
      "needWpm": 136
    },
    {
      "id": "V9",
      "text": "Neighborline is open source. Try the hotline yourself, no login, at the link below. Because the morning after a storm, help should sound like your own language.",
      "start": "2:30.0",
      "end": "2:41.0",
      "window": 11,
      "words": 27,
      "wpm": 150,
      "estSeconds": 10.8,
      "fits": true,
      "needWpm": 147
    }
  ],
